      "rationale": "The certified inclusion reversal motivates recomputed include-root and skip-root completion features. Their difference is sensitive to compatible residual topology; the cover gap moderates reliance on a particular greedy completion. These are heuristic scores, not exact conditional optima. Ten-contact destruction targets larger blocked-gain opportunities, followed by ranking-driven construction and shared improving swaps. Three bounded completion queries justify a higher feature allowance but rapid switching after six stagnant trials. Timed-out partial proposals receive no evaluated reward, and all consumed CPU remains charged."
